The NextWindow daemon is proprietary and is not part of this package. The
packaging supports exactly one SMART Board SB480 per computer in this release.

Before attaching the board, copy the original i386 nwfermi_daemon to
/usr/local/sbin/nwfermi_daemon, make it executable, and review
/etc/nwfermi/daemon.conf. Another location is supported by changing DAEMON in
that configuration file; a symbolic link is unnecessary. Do not run the
legacy nwfermi.service at the same time as this udev-activated integration.

The udev rule matches only USB vendor/product 0b8c:0090 and starts the
nwfermi-daemon@nwfermiN.service instance. N is derived from the actual device
node and is passed to the daemon as /instanceId N; it is never derived from
the USB interface minor. A second board is rejected by an atomic runtime
ownership marker and does not stop or replace the first daemon.

The daemon payload supplied with this project is ELF32/i386. The service checks
its ELF class, interpreter `/lib/ld-linux.so.2`, and `ldd` output before it is
started. Install a suitable 32-bit libc runtime (normally `libc6-i386` or
`libc6:i386`, depending on local Ubuntu policy) before connecting the board.
Run `nwfermi-daemonctl check` after configuring DAEMON to perform the same
preflight without starting the daemon.

The daemon double-forks. systemd therefore owns termination through the unit
cgroup (`KillMode=control-group`); the wrapper never guesses a PID from
`/proc`. `SYSTEMD_WANTS` is used only for the add event. A separate remove
rule lets the `BindsTo=dev-%i.device` dependency stop the unit on unplug.
Correct retention of the daemon child in that cgroup must still be verified
with the physical board.
